 It describes the failure, the rollback, the interrupted first attempt and the next steps.\n- The incident request timed out, but INC-0001 shows up in the incident list, so I didn't retry. There's only one incident and one page.\n\n**Still to do**\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019nes2pwaB9R36YGiVWpdhA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011xdnDKEHVEonVNszB93W41", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MJy8gLhBSJJNZFSTRz6GVj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SZMQRXE3kjXChw9DcwPZ29", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is now on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01D4NpHgAVmLnAp8kboPSnuY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PQ9BiLc1g5yZtSyzCMTxUU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UFTD1bLCU4qWDBYMDgriCg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0165gbsnQ15nBjtxe6YDWp5M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api began failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy in the deploy history. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0143KfvF2oCruuXPQVcStR2f", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The deploy history shows v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to the same version twice is harmless, so I retried once, and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now.\n- After the rollback, the service reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api, which pages the on-call engineer). It describes the failure, the rollback, the interrupted first attempt and the next steps.\n- The incident request timed out, but INC-0001 shows up in the incident list, so I didn't retry. There's only one incident and one page.\n\n**Still to do**\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}